  FT["BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489"] = {"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-11","articleCount":13,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"儿童与青少年咨询委员会条例 2010","en":"CHILDREN AND YOUNG PERSONS ADVISORY BOARDS REGULATIONS 2010","orig":"CHILDREN AND YOUNG PERSONS ADVISORY BOARDS REGULATIONS 2010","vi":"Quy định Ban tư vấn về trẻ em và người chưa thành niên năm 2010","th":"ข้อบังคับคณะกรรมการที่ปรึกษาเด็กและเยาวชน พ.ศ. 2553","id":"Peraturan Dewan Penasihat Anak dan Remaja Tahun 2010","ms":"Peraturan Lembaga Penasihat Kanak-Kanak dan Orang Muda 2010"},"level":"regulation","status":"active","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-REGULATIONS-2010.pdf》（5 页），本次切分 13 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-REGULATIONS-2010.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"These Regulations may be cited as the Children and Young Persons (Advisory Boards) Regulations, 2010 and shall commence on the same date as the Children and Young Persons Order, 2006. Interpretation."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires \"advisory board\" means an advisory board appointed under section 83(4) of the Order; \"home\" means an approved home established under Part XII of the Order; \"resident\" means any child or young person for the time being detained under the Order in a school or home; \"school\" means an approved school established under Part XII of the Order; \"Superintendent\" means the Superintendent in charge of and having the management and control of any school or home and includes any person appointed by the Director to exercise the duties of the Superintendent in his absence. Constitution of advisory board."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"11 Every advisory board shall consist of - J {a} a Chairman; fbi a Vice-Chairman; and {c) such number of other members as the Minister may appoint. {2) At least one of the members of every advisory board shall be a nominee of the Director.\n\n(3) The Minister may at any time revoke the appointment of any member of an advisory board. Chairman."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"(1} The Minister shall appoint one of the members to be the Chairman.\n\n(2) The Chairman shall preside at all meetings of the advisory board. Vice-Chairman."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"( 1) The Vice-Chairman shall be elected by the advisory board from amongst its members.\n\n(2) In the absence of the Chairman, the Vice-Chairman shall preside at all meetings of the advisory board and may exercise all the powers and functions of the Chairman. Secretary."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"The Director shall appoint a Secretary to each advisory board, except that the person appointed shall not {a) be a member; or {b) vote at any proceedings. Term of office."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"(1) Each member of an advisory board shall hold office for a period of not more than 2 years from the date of his appointment and shall be eligible for re-appointment on completion of that period, unless - {a) he resigns during his term of office; or {b) his appointment is revoked by the Minister under regulation 3(3).\n\n(2) A member may resign at any time by giving notice in writing to the Minister.\n\n(3) If a member dies, resigns, has his appointment revoked by the Minister under regulation 3(3) or otherwise vacates his office before the expiry of the term for which he has been appointed, the Minister may appoint any other person to fill the vacancy for so long as the member in whose place that person is appointed would have held office. (4J An advisory board shall not be precluded from holding a meeting or acting in any matter merely by reason of any vacancy in its membership. Meetings."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"[1) An advisory board shall meet as often as may be required, but in any case, at least once in every 3 months.\n\n(2) The quorum at every meeting shall be two-thirds of the number of members.\n\n(3) No business of an advisory board shall be transacted at any meeting thereof unless a quorum is present.\n\n(4) Every question corning before or arising at any meeting of an advisory board shall be decided by a majority of members present and voting thereon at the meeting and, in the case of an equality of votes, the Chairman or, in his absence, the Vice-Chairman shall have a casting vote. Attendance of Superintendent and staff of school or home at meeting of advisory board."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"heading":{"en":"Attendance of Superintendent and staff of school or home at meeting of"},"text":{"en":"The Superintendent and the members of the staff of a school or horne shall attend any meeting held by the advisory board appointed in respect of that school or horne if required by the advisory board to do so. Functions of advisory board."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"text":{"en":"(1) Every advisory board shall, as often as is practicable, review the case of every resident of each school or horne in respect of which it is appointed, and advise the Director as to the suitability of any resident to be released on licence under section 83 of the Order. [2) The Superintendent of every school or horne shall submit to the advisory board appointed in respect thereof, such number of copies of any record report or other document as may be required by the advisory board for the 1 discharge of its duties under the Order or these Regulations. Interview with parents, guardian or relatives of residents."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"text":{"en":"No member shall visit or interview the parent, guardian, sibling or any other member of the family of any resident of any school or home in respect of which the advisory board is appointed without the prior approval of the advisory board. Superintendent of school or home to assist members of advisory board."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"The Superintendent of a school or home shall use his best endeavours to assist any member of the advisory board appointed in respect of the school or home in the exercise of his powers and the discharge of his functions under the Order or these Regulations. Offence and penalty."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-ADVISORY-BOARDS-D59489-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"text":{"en":"The manager and any member of the staff of a school or home who{a) refuses or fails without reasonable cause to allow any member of the advisory board appointed in respect of the school or home access to any record, report or other document relating to any resident of the school or home; {b) refuses or fails without reasonable cause to give any information regarding any resident of the school or home as and when required by a member of the advisory board; or {c) otherwise hinders or obstructs a member of the advisory board in the performance of his duties or the exercise of his powers, is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000. Made this 11th. day of Rabiulawal, 1431 Hijriah corresponding to the 25th. day of February, 2010.\n\nPEHIN ORANG KAYA SETIA PAHLAWAN DATO SERI SETIA DR. AWANG HAJI AHMAD BIN HAJIJUMAT Minister of Culture, Youth and Sports, Brunei Darussalam."}}],"pack":"bn-p28","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"CHILDREN AND YOUNG PERSONS ADVISORY BOARDS REGULATIONS 2010","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-35-2012-E-EMPLOYMENT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2012-1"] = {"id":"BN-S-35-2012-E-EMPLOYMENT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2012-1","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-11","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"就业修正命令 2012(1)","en":"Employment Amendment Order 2012(1)","orig":"Employment Amendment Order 2012(1)","vi":"Sắc lệnh sửa đổi Sắc lệnh Việc làm số 1 năm 2012","th":"คำสั่งแก้ไขเพิ่มเติมคำสั่งการจ้างงาน ฉบับที่ 1 พ.ศ. 2555","id":"Perintah Perubahan Perintah Ketenagakerjaan Nomor 1 Tahun 2012","ms":"Perintah Pindaan Perintah Pekerjaan Bilangan 1 2012"},"level":"regulation","status":"active","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《s-35-2012-e-employment-amendment-order-2012(1).pdf》（4 页），本次切分 3 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"s-35-2012-e-employment-amendment-order-2012(1).pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-35-2012-E-EMPLOYMENT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2012-1-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Employment (Amendment) Order, 2012 and deemed to have commenced on the 1st. January, 2011. of section 45 of S 37/09."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2012-E-EMPLOYMENT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2012-1-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"Section 45 of the Employment Order, 2009, in this Order referred to as the principal Order, is amended in subsection (1), by inserting the following new paragraph immediately after paragraph (h} \"(haj deductions of contributions payable by an employer on behalf of an under and in accordance with the provisions of the Supplemental Contributory Pensions Order, 2009 (S 58/09);\". of section 91."}},{"id":"BN-S-35-2012-E-EMPLOYMENT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2012-1-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"made under Article 83(3))"},"text":{"en":"Section 91 of the principal Order is amended(a} in subsection (1) -\n\n(i) in paragraph (bJiiiL by deleting the fullstop and substituting a\n\n(ii) by adding the following provisos that in the case of a citizen of Brunei Darussalam or resident, every such female employee shall be entitled to herself from work durjng - {a} the period of 2 weeks immediately before her confinement; and (bj the period of 13 weeks immediately after her confinement: further that in the case of a citizen of Brunei Darussalam or permanent resident, and who suffers from incomplete pregnancy at or above, every such female employee shall be entitled to absent herself from work during - {a} the period of 2 weeks immediately before her confinement; and\n\n(b) the period of 6 weeks immediately after her confinement.\"; (b} in subsection (2) - {i) in paragraph {b), by deleting the fullstop and substituting a colon {ii) by adding the following provisos\"Provided that in the case of a citizen of Brunei Darussalam or resident, every such female employee shall be entitled to payment from her employer at her gross rate of pay for the weeks referred to in paragraph fa) of the proviso in\n\n(1) and the first 11 weeks of the period referred to in\n\n(b) of the proviso in subsection (1): further that in the case of a citizen of Brunei Darussalam or permanent resident, who suffers from incomplete pregnancy at 24 weeks or above, every such female employee shall be entitled to payment from her employer at her gross rate of pay for the {c) by adding the following two new subsections\"(5) In this section, \"citizen of Brunei Darussalam or permanent resident\" means a citizen of Brunei Darussalam or a permanent whofa) is an employee in respect of whom contributions are payable by her employer on behalf of the employee under and in accordance with the provisions of the Tabung Amanah Pekerja Act (Chapter 167); and\n\n(b) is lawfully married or validly married under any written law.\n\n(6) The Minister may, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, by order in writing exempt any employee or class of employee from the provision of subsection (5).\". day of Jamadilawal, 1433 Hijriah corresponding to the 24th. day of March, 2012 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN\n\nBRUNEI DARUSSALAM oleh AWANG ABDUL HAMID BIN ABDULLAH, Pemangku Pengarah Percetakan, di Jabatan Percetakan Kerajaan, Bandar Seri Begawan BB3510, Negara Brunei Darussalam. B$5.00"}}],"pack":"bn-p28","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"Employment Amendment Order 2012(1)","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
