  FT["BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04"] = {"id":"BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-11","articleCount":8,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"文莱达鲁萨兰国与印度尼西亚共和国所得税避免双重征税协定命令 2002","en":"INCOME TAX BRUNEI DARUSSALAM THE REPUBLIC OF INDONESIA AODTA ORDER 2002","orig":"INCOME TAX BRUNEI DARUSSALAM THE REPUBLIC OF INDONESIA AODTA ORDER 2002","vi":"Sắc lệnh Thuế thu nhập: Hiệp định tránh đánh thuế hai lần Brunei Darussalam — Cộng hòa Indonesia năm 2002","th":"คำสั่งภาษีเงินได้: ความตกลงการเว้นการเก็บภาษีซ้อนบรูไนดารุสซาลาม — สาธารณรัฐอินโดนีเซีย พ.ศ. 2545","id":"Perintah Pajak Penghasilan: Persetujuan Penghindaran Pajak Berganda Brunei Darussalam — Republik Indonesia Tahun 2002","ms":"Perintah Cukai Pendapatan: Persetujuan Elakan Cukai Dua Kali Brunei Darussalam — Republik Indonesia 2002"},"level":"regulation","status":"active","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-37_2002_E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-OF-INDONESIA-AODTA-ORDER-2002.pdf》（27 页），本次切分 8 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-37_2002_E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-OF-INDONESIA-AODTA-ORDER-2002.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"behalf of each Contracting State irrespective of the manner in which they are"},"text":{"en":"In this Agreement, unless the context otherwise requires -\n\n(a) the term \"Brunei\" meansthe territory of Brunei Darussalam as defined in its laws and the adjacent areas over which Brunei Darussalam has sovereignty, sovereign rights or jurisdiction in accordance with the provisions of the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, 1982;\n\n(b) the term \"Indonesia\" means - the territory of the Republic of Indonesia as defined in its laws and the adjacent areas over which the Republic of Indonesia has sovereignty, sovereign rights or jurisdiction in accordance with the provisions of the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, 1982;\n\n(c) the term \"Government\" means -\n\n(i) in the case of Brunei Darussalam -\n\n(1) The Brunei Currency Board;\n\n(2) The Brunei Investment Agency;\n\n(3) Any local or statutory authority or body exempt from tax in Brunei Darussalam; SCHEDULE-(continued)\n\n(4) Any body corporate controlled or wholly owned by the Government of Brunei Darussalam;\n\n(5) Such institutions as may be agreed from time to time between the two Contracting States;\n\n(ii) in the case of Indonesia -\n\n(1) Local authorities;\n\n(2) A political subdivision;\n\n(3) The Central Bank or any financial institution controlled by the Government the capital of which is wholly owned by the Government;\n\n(d) the terms \"a Contracting State\" and \"the other Contracting State\" mean Brunei or Indonesia as the context requires;\n\n(e) the term \"tax\" means Brunei tax or Indonesian tax as the context reqUIres;\n\n(f) the term \"person\" includes an individual, a company, a body of persons and any other entity which is treated as a taxable entity under the tax laws of the respective Contracting States;\n\n(g) the term \"company\" means any company, body corporate or any other entity which is treated as a company under the tax laws of the respective Contracting States;\n\n(h) the terms \"enterprise of a Contracting State\" and \"enterprise of the other Contracting State\" mean respectively an enterprise carried on by a resident of a Contracting State and an enterprise carried on by a resident of the other Contracting State;\n\n(i) the term \"national\" means -\n\n(i) a) in the case of Brunei Darussalam - any natural person who is afforded the status of a national under the applicable laws in Brunei and may also include any person in possession of a national passport issued by the competent authorities; SCHEDULE-(continuedJ hJ in the case of Indonesia - any natural person who is afforded the status of a national under the applicable laws in Indonesia;\n\n(ii) any legal person, partnership and association deriving its status as such from the laws in force in a Contracting State; (jJ the term \"international traffic\" means carriage of passengers, mails, livestock or goods by a ship or aircraft which is operated by an enterprise of one of the Contracting States, except when the ship or aircraft is operated solely between places in the other Contracting State or solely between such places and one or more structures used for the exploration or exploitation of natural resources situated in waters adjacent to the territorial waters of that other Contracting State; (kJ the term \"competent authority\" means -\n\n(i) in Brunei: the Minister of Finance or his authorised representative;\n\n(ii) in Indonesia: the Minister of Finance or his authorised representative."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"imposed on total income and total capital gains or on elements of income and"},"text":{"en":"As regards the application of this Agreement by a Contracting State, any term not otherwise defined shall, unless the context otherwise requires, have the meaning which it has under the laws of that Contracting State relating to the taxes which are the subject of this Agreement.\n\nARTICLE 4 Resident"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"The existing taxes on which this Agreement shall apply are -"},"text":{"en":"Where by reason of the provisions of paragraph 1 a person other than an individual is a resident of both Contracting States, then it shall be deemed to be a resident of the State in which the control and management of its business is exercised. If its place of control and management cannot be determined, the competent authorities of the Contracting States shall settle the question by mutual agreement.\n\nARTICLE 5 Permanent Establishment"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"which are subsequently imposed in addition to, or in place of, the existing taxes"},"text":{"en":"Notwithstanding the provisions of paragraphs 1 and 2, where a person other than an agent of an independent status to whom paragraph 5 applies is acting in a Contracting State on behalf of an enterprise of the other Contracting State, that enterprise shall be deemed to have a permanent establishment in the firstmentioned Contracting State in respect of any activities which that person undertakes for the enterprise, if such a person - SCHEDULE-{continued}\n\n(a) has and habitually exercises in that Contracting State an authority to conclude contracts in the name of the enterprise, unless the activities of such person are limited to those mentioned in paragraph 3 which, if exercised through a fixed place of business would not make this fixed place of business a permanent establishment under the provisions of that paragraph;\n\n(b) has no such authority, but habitually maintains in the firstmentioned Contracting State a stock of goods or merchandise from which he regularly delivers goods or merchandise on behalf of the enterprise; or\n\n(e) manufactures or processes in that Contracting State for the enterprise goods or merchandise belonging to the enterprise."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"it appears desirable to amend any article of this Agreement without affecting the"},"text":{"en":"An insurance enterprise of a Contracting State shall, except with regard to reinsurance, be deemed to have a permanent establishment in the other Contracting State if it collects premiums in that other State or insures risks situated therein through an employee or through a representative who is not an agent of an independent status within the meaning of paragraph 6."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"An enterprise of a Contracting State shall not be deemed to have a permanent establishment in the other Contracting State merely because it carries on business in that other Contracting State through a broker, general commission agent or any other agent of an independent status, provided that such persons are acting in the ordinary course of their business. However, when the activities of such an agent are devoted wholly or almost wholly on behalf of that enterprise or its associated enterprises, he will not be considered an agent of an independent status within the meaning of this paragraph."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"The fact that a company which is a resident of a Contracting State controls or is controlled by a company which is a resident of the other Contracting State, or which carries on business in that other Contracting State (whether through a permanent establishment or otherwise), shall not of itself make either company a permanent establishment of the other.\n\nARTICLE 6 Income from ImmovableProperty"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2002-E-INCOME-TAX-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-THE-REPUBLIC-19DB04-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"The rate of tax in paragraph 2 and in paragraph 7 of this Article shall not affect the rate of the tax applied in any production sharing contracts or any other similar contracts relating to oil and gas sector or other mining sector concluded by the Government of a Contracting State, its instrumentality, its relevant state oil and gas company or any other entity thereof with a person who is a resident of the other Contracting State.\n\nARTICLE 11 Interest"}}],"pack":"bn-p28","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"INCOME TAX BRUNEI DARUSSALAM THE REPUBLIC OF INDONESIA AODTA ORDER 2002","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD"] = {"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-11","articleCount":86,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"儿童与青少年核准学校与核准收容所条例 2010","en":"CHILDREN AND YOUNG PERSONS APPROVED SCHOOLS AND APPROVED HOMES REGULATIONS 2010","orig":"CHILDREN AND YOUNG PERSONS APPROVED SCHOOLS AND APPROVED HOMES REGULATIONS 2010","vi":"Quy định Trường giáo dưỡng và cơ sở giáo dưỡng được phê duyệt cho trẻ em và người vị thành niên năm 2010","th":"ข้อบังคับโรงเรียนและสถานรับเลี้ยงที่ได้รับอนุมัติสำหรับเด็กและเยาวชน พ.ศ. 2553","id":"Peraturan Sekolah dan Panti yang Disetujui bagi Anak dan Remaja Tahun 2010","ms":"Peraturan Sekolah dan Rumah Diluluskan bagi Kanak-Kanak dan Orang Muda 2010"},"level":"regulation","status":"active","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-AND-APPROVED-HOMES-REGULATIONS-2010.pdf》（29 页），本次切分 86 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-AND-APPROVED-HOMES-REGULATIONS-2010.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"These Regulations may be cited as the Children and Young Persons (Approved Schools and Approved Homes) Regulations, 2010 and shall commence on the same date as the Children and Young Persons Order, 2006. Interpretation."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires - \"advisory board\" means an advisory board appointed under section 83(3) of the Order; \"Assistant Superintendent\" means a person appointed under regulation 3(2); \"Assistant Warden\" means a person appointed under regulation 3(2); \"home\" means an approved home appointed under Part XII of the Order; \"medical officer\" means a medical officer, as defined in section 2(1) of the Order, appointed by the Director-General of Medical Services as medical officer of a school or home; \"resident\" means a child or young person for the time being detained under the Order in the school or home; \"school\" means an approved school appointed under Part XII of the Order; \"Superintendent\", in relation to a school or home, means the Superintendent appointed under regulation 3(2) who is exercising jurisdiction over that school or home; \"Warden\" in relation to a school or home, means the Warden appointed under regulation 3(2} who is exercising jurisdiction over that school or home. Administration."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"( 1} A school or home shall be under the general charge and administration of a Warden, who shall be subject to and comply with such directions as may be given to him by the Superintendent.\n\n(2) The Minister, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, shall appoint for each school or home, a Superintendent, a Warden and such number of Assistant Superintendents, Assistant Wardens and other officers as he may consider necessary.\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES OF SUPERINTENDENT AND WARDEN Responsibilities of Superintendent."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Superintendent shall be responsible to the Director for the proper management of the school or home under his charge, and for the reception, discipline, welfare and rehabilitation of its residents.\n\n(2) The Superintendent shall, with the approval of the Director, determine and draw up the following {a} the duties of the members of the staff of the school or home under his charge; {b} security and other safety measures; and {c} such other standing instructions, duties, programmes and schedules as the Director may direct. Responsibilities of Warden."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"11) The Warden shall be responsible for the maintenance of discipline in the school or home.\n\n(2) The Warden shall also be responsible for all property in the school or home and shall keep the following records - {a} an inventory of the furniture and tools in the school or home; {bj a diary in which all occurrences of importance within the school or home must be recorded; {cj a nominal record of each resident committed to the school or home, showing the date and period of his commitment, the names and addresses of his parents {if known), his distinguishing marks, general appearance, race, language, nationality, apparent age, health, height and weight; {d) a record of the conduct and health of residents while in the school or home;\n\n(e) a punishment book in which all punishments shall be recorded; ff! a book for the entry of observations by members of the advisory board.\n\n(3) In the absence of the Warden, an Assistant Warden shall have the powers and duties of the Warden.\n\n(4) The Warden and the Assistant Warden shall not be absent from the school or home at the same time.\n\n(5) The Assistant Warden and the subordinate staff of the school or home shall be under the orders of the Warden.\n\n(6) The Warden may, subject to the provisions of these Regulations, inflict punishment where it appears necessary and it should be inflicted immediately. General duties."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"( 1) The Warden shall exercise close and constant personal supervision of the school or home. He shall visit and inspect daily all parts of the school or home every day, and shall give special attention to a resident who is confined to his room, and to a resident who is a hospital patient.\n\n(2) The Warden shall visit the school or home during the night. Such visits shall be made at varying intervals and at varying times and not less often than twice a fortnight.\n\n(3) The Warden shall interview a resident as soon as possible after his reception, and prior to his discharge. Warden to carry out recommendations of medical officer."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"The Warden shall, so far as practicable, carry into effect any written recommendation made by the medical officer on grounds of health for the alteration of the discipline or treatment of any resident, or for his separation from other residents. Warden to inform relatives of resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"When a resident is, in the opinion of the medical officer, dangerously ill/ the Warden shall whenever practicable forthwith inform the relatives of such resident. Warden to report cases of insanity."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"The Warden shall, without delay, report to the Superintendent or Assistant Superintendent any case of insanity or apparent insanity occurring among the residents, or any case in which the medical officer has submitted a report under regulations 73(1) and (2l and regulation 74[2). Warden to maintain school or home in proper order."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"The Warden shall pay attention to the ventilation, drainage and sanitary condition of the school or home, and take such measures as may be necessary for their being maintained in proper order. Warden to notify Coroner of death of resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"Upon the death of a resident/ the Warden shall give immediate notice thereof to the Coroner having jurisdiction in respect of such death, to the Superintendent and where practicable, to the nearest relative of the deceased. Inquest on resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Warden shall supply to the Coroner the name of any resident who can give relevant evidence in an inquest about to be held into the death of a resident.\n\n(2) After any inquest on a resident, the Warden shall report to the Superintendent the finding of the inquest and such other circumstances of importance as may arise at the inquest. Visitors to school or home."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Superintendent and the Warden may, in the exercise of their respective discretions, allow any person to visit the school or home.\n\n(2) No person visiting a school or home shall, without the permission of the Warden, make any sketch or take any photograph, and this permission shall not be granted unless an undertaking is given that the sketch or photograph will not be published without the authority of the Superintendent. Removal of visitors for misconduct."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"The Warden may remove from the school or home any visitor whose conduct is improper. Fire precautions."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"The Warden shall take care that proper precautions against fire are adopted, and that the appliances for the extinction of fire are at all times kept in good order and ready for use. He shall take care that instructions are given as to the steps to be taken in case of fire, and that all officers are acquainted with their duties in such an event.\n\nSTAFF Officers to conform to rules and regulations."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"Ill An officer shall conform to the rules and regulations of the school or home and shall support the Warden in the maintenance thereof.\n\n(2) An officer shall obey the lawful instructions of the Warden.\n\n(3) An officer shall report to the Warden any abuse or impropriety which may come to his know ledge. No absence without leave."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"No officer shall be absent from the school or home without leave of the Warden. Health of resident to be brought to notice of Warden."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"An officer shall direct the attention of the Warden to any resident, whether he complains or not, who appears to be unwell, or whose state of mind appears to be deserving of special notice and care. The Warden shall without delay bring such cases to the notice of the medical officer. Officers dealing with resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"(1) No officer, in dealing with a resident, shall use force unnecessarily. In any case in which the application of force to a resident is necessary, no more force than is reasonable shall be used.\n\n(2) No officer shall deliberately act in a manner calculated to provoke a resident.\n\n(3) No officer shall discuss his duties or any matter of discipline or of the school or home arrangements within the hearing of a resident.\n\n(4) No officer shall deal with a resident for an improper purpose. Officers not to act on behalf of any resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"(1) No officer shall, without the authority of the Superintendent carry out any pecuniary or business transaction with, or on behalf of, a resident.\n\n(2) No officer shall, without the authority of the Warden, bring in or carry out, or attempt to bring in or carry out, or knowingly allow to be brought in or carried out, to or from a resident any article whatsoever. Officers not to receive fees."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"No officer shall receive any fee, gratuity or other consideration in connection with the admission of any visitor to a school or home. Communication with ex-resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"No officer shall communicate with an ex-resident or with the friends or relatives of an resident or ex-resident, except with the knowledge of the Warden. Officers to have no dealings with contractors."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"No officer shall, directly or indirectly, have any interest in any contract in connection with a school or home, nor shall he receive, directly or indirectly, under any pretence whatever, any fee, gratuity or other consideration from any contractor or from any person tendering or any other person whatever in connection with any such contract. Officers to submit to search."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"An officer of the school or home shall submit himself to be searched in the school or home if called upon to do so by the Warden. Officers not to communicate with press."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"( 1) No officer shall, directly or indirectly, make any unauthorised communication to any representative of the press or to any other person on matters which have become known to him in the course of his duties.\n\n(2) No officer shall, without the authority of the Superintendent, publish any matter, or make any public pronouncement relating to, a school or home or any resident. Officers' quarters."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"(1) An officer shall occupy such quarters as may be assigned to him; and shall vacate them, if required to do so by the Superintendent.\n\n(2) On the termination of an officer's service, he shall vacate the quarters he has occupied when required to do so. On the death of an officer, his family shall vacate the quarters, when required to do so.\n\nACCOMMODATION Accommodation."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"jl) A room or dormitory shall not be used for the accommodation of residents, unless it is certified by the Superintendent, on the advice of a medical officer, to be of such a size, and to be lit, ventilated and equipped in such a manner, as may be requisite for health.\n\n(2) The certificate shall specify the maximum number of residents to be accommodated at any one time in such room or dormitory, and the number so specified shall not be exceeded. In special circumstances, with the authority of the Superintendent, residents may be located in tents. Accommodation by night."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"Residents may be accommodated by night in rooms or dormitories with not less than 3 residents in each room or dormitory. Each resident shall be provided with a separate bed. Place for sick resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"Sufficient accommodation for the reception, accommodation and treatment of a sick resident shall be provided in a school or home. Female resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"(1) Female residents shall be accommodated entirely separately from male residents.\n\n(2) Where a part of a school or home which contains both male and female residents has been set apart for female residents, that part shall be in the charge of a female officer. It shall be entirely separate from the other part and shall be secured by locks, of which the keys shall be under the exclusive control of female officers.\n\nPARTV\n\nADMISSION, DISCHARGE AND REMOVAL Admission and search of resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Warden shall, upon the delivery to him of a detention order, make all necessary arrangements for the conveyance of the resident named therein to the school or home.\n\n(2) A resident shall be searched on admission and at such times subsequently as may be directed, and all unauthorised articles shall be taken from him.\n\n(3) The searching of a resident shall be conducted in as seemly a manner as is consistent with the necessity of discovering any concealed article.\n\n(4) A female resident shall be searched by only by a female officer. Resident's property."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A32","no":32,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 32."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"All money, clothing or other effects belonging to a resident which he is not allowed to retain shall be placed in the custody of the Warden, who shall keep an inventory thereof, which shall be signed by the resident. Particulars of resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A33","no":33,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 33."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"On admission, and from time to time as may be required, every resident shall be photographed and his name, age, height, weight, distinguishing and other measurements and particulars shall be recorded in such a manner as may be directed. Medical examination on admission."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A34","no":34,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 34."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"A resident shall, on the day of his reception or as soon as possible thereafter, be examined by the medical officer. Bath on reception."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A35","no":35,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 35."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"A resident may be required to have a bath on the day of his reception, unless it is otherwise directed in any particular case by the Warden or medical officer. Diseases on admission."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"If a resident is found to have any infectious or contagious disease or to be in a verminous condition, steps shall at once be taken to treat the disease or condition and to prevent it from spreading to other residents. Notification of rules."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A37","no":37,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 37."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"The Warden shall see a resident on reception and explain to him the rules of the school or home. Medical examination before transfer or discharge."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A38","no":38,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 38."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"A resident shall be examined by the medical officer before being discharged, or removed to another school or home. No resident shall be removed to any other school or home unless the medical officer certifies that he is fit for removal. No resident who is suffering from any acute or dangerous illness shall be discharged from the school or home until, in the opinion of the medical officer, it is safe to do so or, his sentence having expired, he refuses to stay. Privacy during transfer."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A39","no":39,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 39."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"A resident shall be exposed to public view as little as possible while being removed from, or taken to, a school or home. Custody outside school or home."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A40","no":40,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 40."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"A resident, for whose production at any place an order is issued, shall, while outside the school or home, remain in the lawful custody of the officers directed to convey him to that place. Children of female resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A41","no":41,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 41."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"Subject to such conditions as may be prescribed by the Superintendent, the infant child of a female resident may be received into a school or home with its mother, and may be supplied with clothing and necessaries at the expense of the Government.\n\nPROHIBITED ARTICLES Possession."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A42","no":42,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 42."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"No resident shall have in his possession any prohibited article. Any such article which may be found in his possession may be confiscated by the Warden. Conveyance of prohibited articles."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A43","no":43,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 43."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"No person shall, without authority, convey or throw into, or deposit in, a school or home, or convey or throw out of a school or home, or convey to any resident of a school or home, or deposit with a view to its coming into the possession of any such resident, any money, clothing, food, drug, drink, tobacco, letter, paper, book, tool or other article. Anything so conveyed, thrown or deposited without authority may be confiscated by the Warden. Search on entering or leaving."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A44","no":44,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 44."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"Any person or vehicle entering or leaving a school or home may be examined and searched. Any person suspected of bringing any prohibited article into the school or home, or of carrying out any prohibited article or any property belonging to a school or home, shall be stopped, and immediate notice thereof shall be given to the Warden. Liquor."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A45","no":45,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 45."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"No resident shall be given, or allowed to have, any intoxicating liquor. Tobacco."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A46","no":46,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 46."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"No resident shall be allowed to smoke, or to have in his possession any tobacco, except in accordance with such orders as may be given by the Warden.\n\nCLOTHING AND BEDDING Clothing outfit."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A47","no":47,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 47."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"A resident shall be provided with an outfit of clothing adequate for warmth and health in accordance with a scale approved by the Superintendent: Provided that, with the authority of the Warden, other clothing may be worn in special circumstances or if recommended by the medical officer. Bedding scale."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A48","no":48,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 48."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"A resident shall be supplied with bedding adequate for warmth and health in accordance with a scale approved by the Superintendent. Additional bedding may be authorised in special circumstances on the recommendation of the medical officer. Excess prohibited."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A49","no":49,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 49."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"Except as provided in regulations 47 and 48, no resident shall, without the authority of the Warden, receive or have in his possession any clothing, bedding, or equipment, in excess of the authorised allowance. FOOD Diet."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A50","no":50,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 50."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VIII"},"text":{"en":"A resident shall be provided with sufficient and varied food based on a dietary scale recommended by a dietician and approved by the Director. Extra food."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A51","no":51,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 51."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VIII"},"text":{"en":"No resident shall receive, or have in his possession, any food other than the allowance authorised by the dietary scale, except(a) with the authority of the Warden; or\n\n(b) with the authority of the medical officer, if a variation of diet is desirable on medical grounds. Complaints about food."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A52","no":52,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 52."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VIII"},"text":{"en":"A resident who has any complaint to make regarding food supplied to him must make it as soon as possible after the food has been served.\n\nHEALTH AND CLEANLINESS Bath and hair cutting."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A53","no":53,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 53."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IX"},"text":{"en":"A resident shall obey such directions as may be given with regards to washing, bathing, shaving and hair-cutting. Hair cutting of females."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A54","no":54,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 54."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IX"},"text":{"en":"A girl's hair shall not be cut without her consent, unless it is verminous or dirty or when the medical officer considers it requisite on the ground of health. General cleanliness."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A55","no":55,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 55."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IX"},"text":{"en":"A resident shall keep his room, utensils, books and any articles issued for his use and his clothing and bedding, clean and neatly arranged, as may be directed. Exercise."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A56","no":56,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 56."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IX"},"text":{"en":"( 1) A resident, if medically fit, shall be exercised regularly at physical drill and gymnastics.\n\n(2) A resident, unless excused by the medical officer on medical grounds, shall take such other exercise as may be directed.\n\nREHABILITATION AND EDUCATION Rehabilitation programme."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A57","no":57,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 57."},"chapter":{"en":"PART X"},"text":{"en":"(1) The rehabilitation programme for every resident shall, wherever possible, include - {a} moral or religious guidance;\n\n(b) education; {c) vocational training; {d) work; {e) physical training; {f) social and recreational activities; and {g) individual and group therapy.\n\n(2) For the purpose of this regulation, \"work\" means light work, such as making his own bed, cleaning his own dormitory, or assisting in similar light work in the kitchen or about the buildings or grounds of the school or home. Instruction and facilities for religious observance."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A58","no":58,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 58."},"chapter":{"en":"PART X"},"text":{"en":"Instruction and facilities for religious observance shall be provided for all Muslim children. Classes."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A59","no":59,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 59."},"chapter":{"en":"PART X"},"text":{"en":"Provision shall be made for educational classes for the benefit of all residents. Library books."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A60","no":60,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 60."},"chapter":{"en":"PART X"},"text":{"en":"A library of books for the use of residents shall be provided in a school or home. A resident shall be allowed to have not more than 3 library books in his room at any one time and to exchange them as often as may be possible.\n\nVISITS AND COMMUNICATIONS Writing and receipt of letters."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A61","no":61,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 61."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XI"},"text":{"en":"(1) Subject to sub-regulation (3), every resident shall be encouraged to write to his parents, guardian, relatives and friends at least once a month or, if he is unable to write, to dictate his letter to a member of the staff of the school or home.\n\n(2) Subject to sub-regulation (3), every resident shall be allowed to receive letters from his parents, guardian, relatives and friends.\n\n(3) No letter shall be allowed to be posted or received by a resident unless the contents thereof have been screened by the Superintendent or an officer authorised by him. Provision to receive visits."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A62","no":62,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 62."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XI"},"text":{"en":"(1) Subject to sub-regulation (3), every resident shall be allowed to receive visits from his parents or guardian during such hours and at such reasonable intervals as the Director may determine.\n\n(2) The Superintendent may in exceptional cases allow a resident to receive visits from such other persons as the Superintendent thinks necessary or desirable.\n\n(3) The Superintendent may, where the circumstances so warrant, refuse to allow the parents or guardian of a resident to visit him, but in every such case the Superintendent shall record his reasons for doing so in the log book. Home leave."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A63","no":63,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 63."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XI"},"text":{"en":"(1) Every resident may from time to time be granted leave to visit his parents or guardian for such period as the Director may determine. !2) A resident who has been granted leave under sub-regulation (1) shall abide by the following conditions - (a} he shall return to the school or home immediately upon the expiration of the period of leave granted to him; {b} he shall remain indoors during such time as the Director may determine; (c} he shall not visit such places as the Superintendent may specify as being unsuitable for him to visit; fd} he shall not consume or have in his possession any controlled drug, intoxicating substance, tobacco or alcoholic drink; and fe} he shall not behave in a disorderly manner during the period of leave granted to him. Visit by legal adviser."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A64","no":64,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 64."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XI"},"text":{"en":"( 1) Reasonable facilities shall be allowed to the legal adviser of any resident to see him in reference to any legal matters, in the sight but not in the hearing of an officer of the school or home.\n\n(2) For the purpose of this regulation, \"legal adviser\" means the resident's counsel or solicitor, or the clerk of such counsel or solicitor. Visit by police officer."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A65","no":65,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 65."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XI"},"text":{"en":"On production of an order from the proper police authority, a police officer may visit a resident in the school or home, in the sight and hearing of an officer of the school or home.\n\nCOMPLAINTS BY RESIDENT Complaints."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A66","no":66,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 66."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XII"},"text":{"en":"(1) A request by a resident to see the Warden, Superintendent, Director or a member of the advisory board appointed under section 83(4) shall be recorded by the officer to whom it is made and conveyed, without delay, to the Warden, who shall inform the Superintendent or member of the advisory board, as the case may be, of such request.\n\n(2) The Warden shall, at a convenient hour every day, other than Friday, Sunday or public holiday, hear the application of any resident who has requested to see him with a complaint.\n\nGRADES Resident to be divided into grades."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A67","no":67,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 67."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XIII"},"text":{"en":"Ill A resident may be placed in the Penal Grade by order of the Warden, if he is satisfied that such resident is exercising a bad influence or is idle or illconducted. No resident shall be detained in it longer than is necessary in the interests of himself or others.\n\n(2) A resident shall not be promoted in grade, except after full consideration of the circumstances of his case by a committee composed of such officers as the Superintendent may decide. The committee may also order reversion to a lower grade if, for some reason other than an act of misconduct, they consider it desirable.\n\nMEDICAL OFFICER General duties."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A68","no":68,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 68."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XIV"},"text":{"en":"The medical officer shall have the general care of the health of the residents. If practicable he shall visit the school or home daily. Report by medical officer."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A69","no":69,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 69."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XIV"},"text":{"en":"The medical officer shall report to the Superintendent or Assistant Superintendent, through the Warden, any circumstances connected with school or home or the treatment of the residents, which, at any time, appears to him to require consideration on medical grounds. Visits by medical officer."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A70","no":70,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 70."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XIV"},"text":{"en":"(1) The medical officer shall visit the school or home at such times as may be determined by the Director-General of Medical Services.\n\n(2) The medical officer shall examine a resident as soon as possible after his admission and before discharge. On each occasion, the medical officer shall record the health of the resident and such particulars as may be determined by the Superintendent.\n\n(3) The medical officer shall see a resident who complains of illness, and shall report his fitness to the Warden in writing. The medical officer shall visit a sick resident at such times as may be necessary. The medical officer shall attend as soon as is practicable on receiving information of the serious illness of any resident.\n\n(4) The medical officer shall visit a resident under restraint, confined to a room or on restricted diet, and any other resident to whom his attention is specially directed. (5} When a resident is about to be removed from the school or home, the medical officer shall examine him and certify as to his fitness to travel and on such other matters regarding him as may be required.\n\n(6) The medical officer shall, subject to the approval of a Warden, examine at any time, the provisions made for cleanliness and sanitation and examine that they are in efficient working order. He shall report to the Warden any defect or insufficiency therein.\n\n(7) The medical officer shall keep a record of the death of any resident, including(a) the time and date when the deceased was taken ill and when the illness was first notified to him;\n\n(b) the nature of the illness;\n\n(c) the time and date of the death; and\n\n(d) an account of the results of any post-mortem examination made and any special remarks that appear to him to be required. Quarterly inspection."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A71","no":71,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 71."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XIV"},"text":{"en":"Once every 3 months, the medical officer shall inspect every part of the school or home, for the purpose of ascertaining that nothing exists therein likely to be injurious to the health of the residents, and, especially, that the ventilation is sufficiently provided for and properly maintained. The result of each inspection shall be reported to the Superintendent. Food inspection."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A72","no":72,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 72."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XIV"},"text":{"en":"The medical officer shall frequently inspect the residents' food both cooked and uncooked. He shall report to the Warden as to the state and quality of the food, as to any deficiency in the quantity or the quality of the water, as to the sufficiency of clothing and bedding, and on other matters which may affect the health of the residents. Reports on dangers to residents' health."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A73","no":73,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 73."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XIV"},"text":{"en":"( 1) Whenever the medical officer is of the optmon that the health of residents is likely to be injuriously affected by the discipline or treatment of a school or home, he shall report the case in writing, through the Warden, to the Superintendent, together with such recommendations as he thinks proper.\n\n(2) Whenever the medical officer is of the opinion that the life of any resident will be endangered by continued discipline, or that any sick resident will not survive his sentence, or is totally and permanently unfit for training, he shall report his opinion and the grounds thereof in writing, through the Warden to the Superintendent.\n\n(3) Whenever any resident appears to the medical officer to be dangerously ill, he shall give notice thereof to the Warden.\n\n(4) The medical officer shall report in writing to the Warden the case of any resident to which he thinks it necessary, on medical grounds, to draw attention, and shall make such recommendations as he thinks necessary for the alteration of the discipline or treatment of that resident, or for the supply to him of additional articles. Mental health of resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A74","no":74,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 74."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XIV"},"text":{"en":"ill The medical officer shall keep under close observation any resident whose mental condition appears to require it. If necessary, he shall take steps as he may consider proper with a view to the segregation or removal of such resident to a school or home designated for the observation of weak-minded residents, or to the certification of the resident under any law relating to mental health or disorder. !2) The medical officer shall report through the Warden, to the Superintendent, any case of a resident whose mental health appears likely to become impaired by continued discipline or treatment. Contagious diseases."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A75","no":75,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 75."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XIV"},"text":{"en":"The medical officer shall submit to the Warden, in writing a recommendation for separating from other residents any resident suffering, or suspected of suffering, from any infectious or contagious disease, and shall immediately take steps to treat such disease.\n\nDISCIPLINE Reports on resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A76","no":76,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 76."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"text":{"en":"A report against a resident shall be dealt with by the Warden. Resident may be segregated."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A77","no":77,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 77."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"text":{"en":"When a resident has been reported for an offence the Warden rnay order him to be kept apart from other residents, pending adjudication. Resident to be informed of alleged offence."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A78","no":78,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 78."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"text":{"en":"A resident shall, before a report is dealt with, be informed of the offence for which he has been reported and shall be given an opportunity of hearing the facts alleged against him and of being heard in his defence. Offences."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A79","no":79,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 79."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"text":{"en":"A resident is guilty of an offence against school or home discipline if he {a) disobeys an order of the Warden or of any other officer of the school or home;\n\n(b) is idle, careless, negligent at work, or refuses to work; {c) is indecent in language, act or gesture;\n\n(d) escapes from the school or home or from legal custody;\n\n(e) mutinies or incites other resident to mutiny; (fJ commits personal violence against any officer of the school or home, or any other resident;\n\n(g) in any way offends against these regulations or the good order and discipline of the school or home;\n\n(h) attempts to do any of the foregoing things. Punishment by Warden."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A80","no":80,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 80."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Warden may examine any person in relation to any alleged offence against the discipline of the school or home and determine thereupon, and make one or more of the following forms of punishment {a) removal to the Penal Grade; {b) deprivation of any of the following privileges for a period not exceeding one month -\n\n(i) association;\n\n(ii) playing games; {c) loss of stage or grade for a period not exceeding 3 months; {d) confinement to a room for a period not exceeding 3 days; {e) deprivation of a mattress for a period not exceeding 7 days; {f) performance of extra duties in and around the buildings or compound of the school or home. [2) The Superintendent shall record in the discipline book - {a) the reasons for his decision to impose any punishment on any resident; and {b) the form of punishment imposed.\n\n(3) The Superintendent shall inform the resident's parents or guardian as soon as possible of the disciplinary action that has been taken and the punishment that has been imposed. Corporal punishment."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A81","no":81,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 81."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"text":{"en":"{1) The Superintendent and staff of the school or home shall make every effort to enforce discipline without resort to corporal punishment.\n\n(2) No corporal punishment shall be imposed on a resident unless the Superintendent is satisfied after an inquiry that the resident is guilty of serious misconduct and that the misconduct is of such a nature as to warrant the imposition of corporal punishment.\n\n(3) The Superintendent shall record in the discipline book the particulars and evidence of the resident's alleged misconduct, his finding on the evidence, and the grounds of his decision to impose corporal punishment.\n\n(4) Corporal punishment shall be administered only on the following conditions - (a} where corporal punishment is to be administered to a male resident(i) it shall be administered by the Superintendent or an officer authorised by him in the presence of another officer who shall sign in the punishment book as a witness to the carrying out of the punishment;\n\n(ii) it shall be inflicted with a cane of a type approved by the Director;\n\n(iii) the number of strokes inflicted shall not exceed 12;\n\n(iv) the strokes may be inflicted on the resident's palm or on his buttocks over his ordinary cloth shorts; and\n\n(v) it shall not be administered in the presence of any other resident; and\n\n(b) where corporal punishment is to be administered to a female resident(i) it shall be administered by the Superintendent or a female officer authorised by him in the presence of another officer who shall sign in the punishment book as a witness to the carrying out of the punishment;\n\n(ii) it shall be inflicted with a cane of a type approved by the Director;\n\n(iii) the number of strokes inflicted shall not exceed 12;\n\n(iv) the strokes shall be inflicted on the resident's palm; and\n\n(v) it shall not be administered in the presence of any other resident.\n\n(5) Corporal punishment shall not be administered to any resident who suffers from any physical or mental disability. [6J In any case in which corporal punishment is administered, the Superintendent shall {a} record in the discipline book, immediately thereafter, such details of the corporal punishment as may be required by the Director; and {b) as soon as possible thereafter report the facts and circumstances of the case to the Director. Prohibition of unauthorised forms of corporal punishment."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A82","no":82,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 82."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"text":{"en":"[ 1 J Except as provided under regulation 81, no member of the staff of a school or home shall subject any resident to any form of corporal punishment.\n\n(2) For the purpose of this regulation, \"corporal punishment\" includes striking, cuffing, shaking or punching a resident, or subjecting him to any other form of physical violence. Requirement of certificate of medical officer that resident is fit to undergo punishment."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A83","no":83,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 83."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"heading":{"en":"Requirement of certificate of medical officer that resident is fit to undergo"},"text":{"en":"Confinement to a room-or corporal punishment shall in no case be ordered unless the medical officer has certified that the resident is in a fit condition of health to sustain it. Visit to resident sentenced to confinement."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A84","no":84,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 84."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"text":{"en":"A resident confined to a room shall be visited {a} at least once a day by the Warden; {b) at intervals of not more than 3 hours each day by the an officer appointed officer by the Warden. Duty of Superintendent upon return of resident who has escaped from school or home."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A85","no":85,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 85."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"heading":{"en":"Duty of Superintendent upon return of resident who has escaped from"},"text":{"en":"Where a resident who has escaped from a school or home returns thereto, the Superintendent shall {a} within 7 days after the return of the resident calculate the period during which the resident was at. large in accordance with section 84(2) of the Order; {b) issue a certificate stating the period during which the resident was at large; (cj cause a copy of the certificate issued under paragraph (bj to be furnished and explained to -\n\n(i) the resident, who shall acknowledge it; and\n\n(ii) the parents or guardian of the resident; and (dJ submit a copy of the certificate to the Juvenile Court. Punishment of resident who has been guilty of escaping from school or home."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2010-CHILDREN-AND-YOUNG-PERSONS-APPROVED-SCHOOLS-3760DD-A86","no":86,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 86."},"chapter":{"en":"PART XV"},"heading":{"en":"Punishment of resident who has been guilty of escaping from school or"},"text":{"en":"Where a resident is guilty of having escaped from a school or home, the Superintendent of the school or home may impose corporal punishment on the resident in accordance with regulation 81. Made this 11th. day of Rabiulawal, 1431 Hijriah corresponding to the 25th. day of February, 2010.\n\nDAYANG HAJAH MISNAH BINTI HAJI BOLHASSAN Acting Director of Community Development, Ministry of Culture, Youth and Sports, Brunei Darussalam."}}],"pack":"bn-p28","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"CHILDREN AND YOUNG PERSONS APPROVED SCHOOLS AND APPROVED HOMES REGULATIONS 2010","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016"] = {"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-11","articleCount":20,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"土地法典修正命令 2016","en":"LAND CODE AMENDMENT ORDER 2016","orig":"LAND CODE AMENDMENT ORDER 2016","vi":"Sắc lệnh sửa đổi Bộ luật Đất đai năm 2016","th":"คำสั่งแก้ไขเพิ่มเติมประมวลกฎหมายที่ดิน พ.ศ. 2559","id":"Perintah Perubahan Kitab Undang-Undang Tanah Tahun 2016","ms":"Perintah Pindaan Kanun Tanah 2016"},"level":"regulation","status":"active","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-37_2016_E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016.pdf》（17 页），本次切分 20 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-37_2016_E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"Citation and commencement"},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Land Code (Amendment) Order, 2016 and shall commence on a date to be appointed by the Minister, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, by notification in the Gazette."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"Insertion of new section 1A into Chapter 40"},"text":{"en":"The Land Code in this Order referred to as the Code, is amended by inserting the following new section immediately after section 1 - . 1A. In this Code, unless the context otherwise requires - \"claim to or interest in any land\" includes a legal or equitable estate established in the land and a right, power or privilege over, in relation \"non-citizen\" means any person who is not a subject 'of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan of Brunei Darussalam; \"to transfer\", with reference to land means to convey, sell, assign, settle, create by declaration of trust, assent or in any manner dispose of any estate or interest in land, and includes the vesting of any estate or interest in land, but does not include a transfer by way of charge, lease or sub-lease and \"transfer\" includes a conveyance, sale, assignment, settlement, declaration of trust, assent, disposition of whatever nature, the vesting of any estate or interest in land by an instrument or under a vesting order of court and every instru~rrent capable of vesting any estate or interest in land upon registration of such ilrstrurrrent in the Register, but does not include a charge, lease"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"Insertion of new sections 3A, 3B and 3C"},"text":{"en":"The Code is amended by inserting the following three new sections immediately after section 3 - 4th. J U N E , 2016 transfer to, or purchase or acquisition by, non-citizen of land etc (a] person shall, whether for consideration or by way of gift vivos or otherwise, transfer any land or any estate or interest a non-citizen;\n\n(b) person shall create any trust in respect of any land or any estate or interest therein in favour of a non-citizen; and\n\n(c) non-citizen shall purchase or acquire any land or any estate or interest therein except by way of a charge, lease or sub-lease.\n\n(a) transfer of any land or any estate or interest therein by any person to a non-citizen made in contravention of subsection (l)(a);\n\n(b) trust in respect of any land or any estate or interest therein created by any person in favour of a non-citizen in contravention of\n\n(l)(b); or\n\n(c) purchase or acquisition of any land or any estate or interest therein by a non-citizen, except by way of a charge, lease or sub-lease made in contravention of subsection (l)(c), shall, whether made before or after the commencement of this Order on or after a date to be notified by the Minister in the Gazette, be null and void.\n\n(3) This section shall apply to a legal person, a statutory body constituted under any written law, a society registered under the Societies 203) and a co-operative society registered under the Cooperative Societies Act (Chapter 84) unless such legal person, statutory body, society and co-operative society is exempted under section 48. Non-citizen to furnish particulars of claim or interest in land 3B. (1) A non-citizen claiming to have any claim to or interest in any land, shall, no later than a date to be notified by the Minister in the Gazette or such further period as the Minister may allow, furnish to the officer in charge of the Land Office a statement setting out the particulars of such claim or interest.\n\n(2) Such officer in charge of the Land Office shall proceed to inquire into such claim or interest in any land and shall refer the matter to His Majesty in Council for direction.\n\n(3) His Majesty in Council may, upon receiving the matter from the officer in charge of the Land Office direct such claim or interest in any land to be alienated to such extent as is allowed by this Code subject to such restrictions and conditions as His Majesty in Council may think proper and the officer in charge of the Land Office shall rectify the Register and the extract of title in accordance with such direction.\n\n(4) The officer in charge of the Land Office shall report to His Majesty in Council the circumstances of any contravention of the provisions of this section. ( 5 ) If His Majesty in Council is satisfied after such inquiry as His Majesty in Council may deem necessary that any provision of this section has been contravened, His Majesty in Council may make a direction in similar terms to subsection (3).\n\n(6) A direction of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan in Council under this section shall be final and shall not be called in question in any court. Succession etc. of land by non-citizen 3C. ( I ) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Code or of any other written law, no claim to or interest in any land belonging to a deceased person shall pass by bequest, succession or inheritance to any non-citizen who is beneficially entitled under a will or under any written law governing intestate succession.\n\n(2) The legal personal representatives to whom probate or letters of administration are granted in respect of such claim to or interest in any land shall within a period of 12 months of the date of the death of the deceased person furnish to the officer in charge of the Land Office a statement setting out the particulars of the land and of any claim to or interest of the non-citizen therein.\n\n(3) Where a non-citizen would, but for subsection (I), be beneficially entitled to any land, the legal personal representatives to whom probate or letters of administration are granted in respect of such land shall, subject to\n\n(4), be bound to sell such land, to a citizen within a period of 5 years of the date of the death of the deceased person and upon such sale to pay, subject to the law of wills and intestate succession, the proceeds thereof, less any expenses necessarily incurred on the such sale or by reason of the administratio11 of a deceased's estate, to or for or on behalf of the non-citizen so beneficially entitled.\n\n(4) Where the legal personal representatives have not sold, or have not been able to sell the land within the period specified in subsection (31, the legal personal representatives or the trustees of the will or estate of the deceased person for the time being shall furnish to the officer in charge of the Land Office (within sucB period not exceeding 6 monlhs as such officer may require) a statement setting out the particulars of the land which has not been sold, giving reasons for their failure or onlissioi~ to sell. ( 5 ) The officer in charge of the Land Office shall, after receipt of such statement or where no such statement has been received within the time specified, seek the direction of [he Minister, and thc Minister lnay issue to the officer a notice to attach and sell the land and a copy of suc,h notice shall be served on -\n\n(a) the legal personal representatives to whom probate or letters of administration have been granted in respect of land in question; and\n\n(b) the subsisting chargees (if any) of the land.\n\n(6) Where the officer in charge of the Land Office has sold the land pursuant to the notice to attach and sell under subsection (5), the officer shall pay the proceeds of the sale less any costs incurred to the legal personal.representatives or the trustees of the will or estate of the deceased person for the time being and upon the acknowledgment of the receipt of such proceeds of sale by the legal personal representatives or the trustees, the officer in charge of the Land Office shall be discharged from all liability in respect of the application of the proceeds of sale; or the officer, if he is unable to make payment of the proceeds of sale and to obtain such acknowledgment as aforesaid, may make payment into court of such proceeds of sale less all costs incurred thereby.\n\n(7) Where payment of the proceeds of sale has been made by the officer in charge of the Land Office as provided in subsection ( 6 ) , every non-citizen beneficially entitled under a will or by intestate succession shall be entitled to receive and shall be paid such proceeds of sale by the legal personal representatives or trustees of the will or estate of the deceased person for the time being, and in any case where the proceeds of sale have been paid into court, that non-citizen shall be entitled to make application to court for payment out of court of the proceeds of sale to be made to him, and the payment of the proceeds of sale in either case shall be in accordance with the terms of the will or the law of wills or intestate succession, as the case may be.\n\n(8) Notwithstanding subsections (3) and (5), the officer in charge of the Land Office may, after receipt of the statement referred to in\n\n(4) and (5), with the approval of the Minister, allow such extension of time, as the officer may think fit, for the sale of such land.\n\n(9) The provisions of this section shall not apply to a non-citizen who is a surviving joint tenant of any land.\n\n(10) In this section, \"letters of administration\" and \"probate\" have the same meanings as in the Probate and Administration Act (Chapter ll).\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"Insertion of new section 32A"},"text":{"en":"The Code is amended by inserting the following new section immediately \"Land not to be purchased or acquired by purchaser as nominee on behalf of another\n\n(a) person shall, purchase or acquire any estate or interest in any land as a nominee with the intention that the person shall hold it on trust for another person; and\n\n(b) person shall authorise or appoint as his nominee any person to purchase or acquire any estate or interest in any land with the intention that such person shall hold it on trust for himself or another except with the prior approval in writing of His Majesty in Council and subject to such restrictions and conditions as His Majesty in Council may\n\n(2) Any trust created in whatever manner or form in contravention of subsection (1) whether made before or after the commencement of this null and void and there shall be no resulting trust in favour of the beneficiary; and any contract or covenant between such person and the beneficiary in respect of such estate to or interest in land shall be null and void.\n\n(3) The Land Officer, upon discovering that any instrument of transfer contains any such void trust and the instrument is pending final registration or has been finally registered by the Land Officer, shall enter a note in that instrument or the registration copy thereof, as the case may be, stating that such trust is nzlll and void by virtue of subsection (2).\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"Insertion of new sections 35 to 49"},"text":{"en":"The Code is amended by inserting the following fifteen new sections in~mediately after sectiurl 34 -"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of Schedule"},"text":{"en":"The Schedule to the Code is amended -\n\n(a) by deleting \"& 23\" from the heading and by substituting \", 23, 35, 38, 41 and 45\" therefor;\n\n(b) by adding the following new Forms - gi? 'd 2 co K * 0- : . e, : 0- 0 : c cp : i & t 3 't , C- D . P. b 5'\n\nFORM H Notice of entry of caveat To ...................... .of .......................... *registered owner of the landlperson having interest in the land .............................. and registered in the Land ............................................ This is to inform you that, in exercise of the powers conferred by sections *38145(2), I have this day entered, upon the Register in respect of the land - *(a) a Land Officer's Caveat. * (b) a caveat on the application of - and the effect thereof is - ........................................... [Here state the effect of the caveat] Dated this ............ day of ............... ......, 20 .......... * Delete as appropriate.\n\nFORM I Notice to Withdraw Caveat To the Land Officer ...................... [Here enter the name of the District as appropriate.] I, ..................... of ...................... being the *person/ personal representative of the person who entered Caveat ............ Folio No ........... against the *land/registered interest described in the Register No. ......................... and registered in the Land Office at .................................... hereby give notice that I wish to withdraw the said caveat under section 41 of the Land Code (Chapter 40)."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A35","no":35,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 35."},"text":{"en":"Any person -\n\n(a) claiming to be entitled to, or to be beneficially interested in, any land, or any interest therein capable of registration under this\n\n(b) who is a guardian of the property of an infant beneficially interested in any land, may apply for the entry of a caveat with the Land Officer in Form G in the Schedule with such variations as circumstances may require\n\n(i) the prescribed fee; and\n\n(ii) the grounds giving rise to the claim by the caveator thereto, verified by a statutory declaration by the applicant or his advocate and solicitor."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36."},"text":{"en":"(1) The Land Officer shall note on any application under section 35 the time at which it was received and, subject to section 44, shall as soon as may be thereafter (and without being concerned to enquire into the validity of the claim on which it is based) give effect thereto by entering the caveat applied for in the manner provided by subsection (2).\n\n(2) The Land Officer shall record the entry of caveat in the Register and the extract of title together with a statement specifying -\n\n(a) the person on whose application it was entered;\n\n(b) the time from which it is effective (being the time of receipt of the application, as noted thereon pursuant to subsection (1)); and\n\n(c) the reference under which the application is filed."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A37","no":37,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 37."},"text":{"en":"So long as a caveat remains in force, the Land Officer shall not make any entry in the Register having the effect of transferring, charging, leasing or sub-leasing or otherwise affecting the interest in respect of which the caveat was entered: Provided that nothing herein shall prevent the recording of a transmission in accordance with section 28 or of any other dealing which has been accepted for registration before receipt of the caveat or to which the caveator has given his written consent. Notice of caveat to be given"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A38","no":38,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 38."},"text":{"en":"Upon the entry of the caveat, the Land Officer shall serve notice in Form H to the registered owner of the land or any other person having a registered interest in the land against which the caveat has been entered. Procedure for removal"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A39","no":39,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 39."},"text":{"en":"(1) Any registered owner or any other person having a registered interest in land against which a caveat has been entered may at any time apply to the High Court for an order that the caveat be removed.\n\n(2) The Court, upon proof that notice of such application has been duly served, may make such order either ex parte or otherwise as is just.\n\n(3) The Land Officer shall, on being duly served with any order under this section for the removal of a caveat, cancel the entry thereof in the Register and the extract of title in accordance with such order."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A40","no":40,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 40."},"text":{"en":"Every caveat shall, if not sooner removed by the Land Officer pursuant to an order under section 39 or withdrawn under section 41, lapse after the 3 years from the time from which it took effect and may, upon payment of the prescribed fee, be renewed for a further period not 3 years. Withdrawal of caveats 4 (1) A caveat may be withdrawn at any time by or on behalf of the caveator by a notice in Form I accompanied by the prescribed fee and presented to the Land Officer.\n\n(2) On receiving any notice of withdrawal under this section, the Land (a/ cancel the entry of thc caveat in thc Register and thc extract of title; and fb/ give notice of the withdrawal to the registered owner or any other person having a registered interest in the land formerly bound by lhe caveal. Compensation for wrongft~l caveats"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A42","no":42,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 42."},"text":{"en":"(1) Any person loligillg a caveat without reasonable cause is liable to pay to any person who suffers any damage or loss thereby such compensation as the Court consider-s just.\n\n(2) Such colnpensation sl-)all be recoverable in an action at law from thc person who entered the cilveilt by the person who st~ffered the damages or losses. Limitation on repeated applications"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A43","no":43,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 43."},"text":{"en":"Where the Court has ordered the removal of ally caveat under 39, or where the Land Officer has cancelled ally caveat pursuant to section 41(2), it shall not be lawful for the Land Officer to receive a second caveat affecting the same land by the same person or in respect of the same right and for the same cause, except by order of the Court. Land Officer's caveat"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A44","no":44,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 44."},"text":{"en":"The Land Officer may enter a caveat -\n\n(a) for the protection of the interests of the Government or the\n\n(b) for securing that the land will be available to satisfy the whole or part of any debt due to the Government;\n\n(c) for the prevention of fraud or improper dealing;\n\n(d) for the protection of any person who is under the disability of , unsoundness of mind, is absent from Brunei Darussalam or is an infant, to prohibit the transfer or other dealing with any interest belonging or supposed to belong to any such person; (el on behalf of any charitable trust or in the interests of any (fl to prohibit the dealing with any land or any interest therein capable of registration under this Code in any case in which it appears to him that an error has been made in any document evidencing title to that land or for the prevention of fraud or improper dealing."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A45","no":45,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 45."},"text":{"en":"(1) A Land Officer's caveat shall be in Form J and the Land Officer shall record the entry of such caveat in the Register and the extract of title.\n\n(2) Upon the entry of the Land Officer's caveat, the Land Officer shall serve notice in Form H to the registered owner of the land or any other person having a registered interest in the land affected by the caveat.\n\n(3) A Land Officer's caveat shall continue in force until it is cancelled by the Land Officer -\n\n(a) of his own motion; or\n\n(b) on an application in that behalf by the registered owner of the land or any other person having a registered interest in the land or estate affected by the caveat; or\n\n(c) pursuant to any order of the Minister made on an appeal under subsection (5) against his decision to enter the caveat, or his refusal of any application for its cancellation under paragraph (b).\n\n(4) Where the Land Officer effects a cancellation under subsection (3), the Land Officer shall cancel the entry thereof in the Register and the extract of title and notify the registered owner of the land or any other person having a registered interest in the land affected by the caveat.\n\n(5) Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Land Officer's caveat under subsection (1) or his refusal to cancel such caveat upon application under subsection 3(b) may, within 30 days of the receipt of the notice referred to in subsection (2), or such extended period of time as the Minister may allow, appeal in writing against such decision to the Minister whose decision thereon shall be final. Diplomatic and consular missions in Brunei Darussalam"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A46","no":46,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 46."},"text":{"en":"(1) Any government of a foreign country or territory outside Brunei Darussalam or any accredited agent of that government which intends to purchase or acquire any land for any diplomatic, consular or official purpose of that government or for the purposes of an official residence for any accredited agent of that government shall first seek the permission in writing of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan in Council for such purchase\n\n(2) The requirement under subsection (1) for the permission in writing of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan in Council shall not apply to the purchase or acquisition (whether by lease, deed of assignment or other a leasehold estate or interest for a term not exceeding 7 years, inclusive of any further term which nlay be granted by way of an option for"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A47","no":47,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 47."},"text":{"en":"Nothing in this Order shall -\n\n(a) affect any transfer of any land to the Official Receiver or trustee in bankruptcy;\n\n(b) prevent the occupation of land as a tenant thereof or from entering into any agreement, whether in writing or otherwise, with the landlord thereof for the occupation of land, or from acquiring any estate or interest under any tenancy agreement, lease or deed of Provided that in every such case no term in any such tenancy agreement, lease or deed of assignment shall exceed a period of 7 years at any one time, inclusive of any further term which may be granted by way of an option for renewal;\n\n(c) prevent the transfer of a claim to or interest in land where -\n\n(i) the prior approval in writing of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan in Council has been obtained; or\n\n(ii) the land forms part of a stratum estate under the Land Code (Strata) Act (Chapter 189)."}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A48","no":48,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 48."},"text":{"en":"His Majesty and Yang Di-Pertuan in Council may, either generally or in any particular case, and either permanently or for such period as His Majesty in Council may think fit, exempt any person or class of persons, from all or any of the provisions of this Code; and in granting such exemption His Majesty and Yang Di-Pertuan in Council may impose such conditions as His Majesty in Council may think proper. Powers of officer in charge of Land Office"}},{"id":"BN-S-37-2016-E-LAND-CODE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A49","no":49,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 49."},"text":{"en":"(1) For the purpose of performing his duties under this Code, the officer in charge of the Land Office may summon any person to give evidence or produce any document or other article in his possession.\n\n(2) Any person who -\n\n(a) refuses to attend upon being summoned;\n\n(b) refuses to furnish any information or produce any document or other article to the officer in charge of the Land Office;\n\n(c) furnishes any information or produces any document which is false in a material particular and which he knows to be false or does not believe to be true; or\n\n(d) obstructs or impedes the officer in charge of the Land Office, is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both.\". of Schedule"}}],"pack":"bn-p28","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"LAND CODE AMENDMENT ORDER 2016","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
