  FT["BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015"] = {"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-11","articleCount":54,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"保险修正命令 2015","en":"INSURANCE AMENDMENT ORDER 2015","orig":"INSURANCE AMENDMENT ORDER 2015","vi":"Sắc lệnh sửa đổi Sắc lệnh Bảo hiểm năm 2015","th":"คำสั่งแก้ไขเพิ่มเติมคำสั่งประกันภัย พ.ศ. 2558","id":"Perintah Perubahan Perintah Asuransi Tahun 2015","ms":"Perintah Pindaan Perintah Insurans 2015"},"level":"regulation","status":"active","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-38_2015_E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015.pdf》（19 页），本次切分 54 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-38_2015_E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Insurance (Amendment) Order, 2015. of section 5 of S 48/2006."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"Section 5 of the Insurance Order, 2006, in this Order referred to as the Order is amended, in subsection (5), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $2,0.00 for every day during the offence continues after conviction\" and by substituting \"a fine not $150,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"Section 6 of the principal Order is amended by deleting \"a fine not exceeding imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day during the offence continues after conviction\" and by substituting \"a fine not $100,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"Section 7 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (3), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $5,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding every day during which the offence continues after conviction\" and by \"a fine not exceeding $50,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not $1,000 for every day during which the offence continues after therefor. lst. 2015"}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"Section 15 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new immediately after subsection ~2} \"(3) Any insurer who contravenes subsection ~1) shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50 000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for day during which the offence continues after conviction.\". of sectionl6."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"Section 16 of the principal Order is amended {a} in subsection (1), by deleting \"prescribed\" from the last line and by \"determined\" therefor; {b} in subsection (2), by deleting \"prescribed\" from the last line and by \"determined\" therefor; {c} in subsection (5)\n\n(i) by inserting \"if\" immediately after \"and\" in the third line;\n\n(ii) \"prescribed\" from the fourth line and by substituting therefor; {d} in subsection (6), by deleting \"prescribed\" from the penultimate line and by substituting \"deterJI?-ined\" therefor; {e} by inserting \"(8)\" immediately before \"Where\" in the fourth last line; (fJ by the new\n\n(8) \"(9) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"Section 18 of the principal Order is amended {a} by inserting \"(1)\" immediately before \"In\" in the first line;\n\n(b) by adding the new after\n\n(1) - \"(2) Any person who fails to comply with subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day during which the offence continues after"}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"Section 20 of the principal Order is amended - (a} in subsection (4), by deleting \"a qualified\" from the third line and by substituting \"an\" therefor;\n\n(b) in subsection (5), by deleting \"a qualified\" from the third line and by substituting \"an\" therefor;\n\n(c) by the new 13) - \"( 14) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"text":{"en":"Section 21 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new immediately after subsection (4) \"[5) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $500,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"text":{"en":"Section 23 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new subsection immediately after subsection (6) - \"(7) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"text":{"en":"Section 24 of the principal Order is amended -\n\n(a) in subsection {1), in paragraph {e), by deleting \"on\" from the second line and by substituting \"of\" therefor; fbJ by the new immediately\n\n(4) - \"(5) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"Section 25 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (6), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years, or both\" and by sub'stituting \"a fine not exceeding $50,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years, or both\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"text":{"en":"Section 27 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (5), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $5,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day during which the offence continues after and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $10,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day during the offence continues after conviction\" therefor. Amendment of section 28."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"text":{"en":"Section 28 of the principal Order is amended{a} in subsection (1), by deleting \"section 19, 20 or 23\" from the first 2lines and by substituting \"section 19 or 20\" therefor; {b) in subsection (2), by deleting \"section 19, 20 or 23\" from the last line and by substituting \"section 19 or 20\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15."},"text":{"en":"Section 29 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (4), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $5,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day during which the offence continues after and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $10,000, and in the case of a offence to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day during the offence continues after conviction\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"text":{"en":"Section 31 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (7), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $10,000\" and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $50,000\""}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17."},"text":{"en":"Section 32 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new immediately after subsection (2) \"(3) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18."},"text":{"en":"Section 33 of the principal Order is amended -\n\n(a) in subsection (4), by inserting a comma immediately after \"policy\" in the second line;\n\n(b) in subsection (7), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $5,000\" and by \"a fine not exceeding $10,000\" therefor. of section 3 7."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19."},"text":{"en":"Section 37 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (1), by inserting a immediately after \"language\" in the penultimate line."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20."},"text":{"en":"Section 38 of the principal Order is amended by deleting \"a fine not imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year, or both\" and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $50,000, imprisonment for a term not one year or both\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21."},"text":{"en":"Section 40 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new immediately after subsection \\2) - \"(3) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000.'~ Amendment of section 41."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22."},"text":{"en":"Section 41 of the principal Order is amended - {a} in subsection jl){a}, by deleting \"prescribed\" and by substituting therefor; fb} by adding the new subsection 5) \"(6) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day during which the offence continues after Amendment of section 42."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23."},"text":{"en":"Section 42 of the principal Order is amended - {a) in subsection (l)(a), by deleting \"prescribed\" and by substituting therefor; {b} in subsection (4), by inserting a comma immediately after \"section\" in the first line therefor; [c) by the new\n\n(4) \"(5) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding Amendment of section 43."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24."},"text":{"en":"Section 43 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (4), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $5,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both\" and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term one year or both\" therefor. Amendment of section 44."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25."},"text":{"en":"Section 44 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new immediately after subsection (2) \"(3) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1 0,000.\". Amendment of section 45."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26."},"text":{"en":"Section 45 of the principal Order is amended faJ in subsection (1), by adding \"and counters\" therefor; {bJ in subsection (4J, by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $20,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day which the offence continues after conviction\" and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $50,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction\" therefor. Substitution of section 46."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27."},"text":{"en":"Section 46 of the principal Order is repealed and the following new section therefor - \"Insurance agents to act only for insurers entitled to ~arry on business in Brunei"}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28."},"text":{"en":"Section 48 of the principal Order is amended {a/ by inserting the following three new subsections immediately after {2) .. (2A) In registering an insurance agent, the Authority may impose such he thinks fit and may at any time add to, vary or revoke such conditions. (2B) The Authority may revoke the registration of any insurance agent if he is satisfied that any of the conditions imposed in relation to the has been breached or that it is in the interests of the public to do so. (2C) The Authority shall cause notice of any registration or of the of any registration of an insurance agent to be published in the Gazette.\";\n\n(b) in subsection (5), by inserting \"registration and annual\" immediately «fees\" therefor; {cj by deleting subsection (9) and by substituting the following new therefor - \"(9) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000, for a term not exceeding 6 months or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29."},"text":{"en":"Section 49 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (2), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $ 10,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both\" and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both,\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30."},"text":{"en":"Section 50 of the principal Order is amended -\n\n(a) in subsection (1) !i) in paragraph (a}, by deleting \"individual\";\n\n(ii) in paragraph (b), by deleting \"a corporate\" and by substituting \"an\" (bJ in subsection (3), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $10,000, for a term not exceeding 6 months or both\" and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31."},"text":{"en":"Section 51 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection {1), by deleting by a fine not exceeding $4,000 for each day on which he is proved to have done so, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both\" and by \"imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $4,000 for every day which the offence continues after conviction\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A32","no":32,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 32."},"text":{"en":"Section 53 of the principal Order is amended {a} by deleting subsection (1) and by substituting the following new therefor - \"(1) No person shall, without being registered by the Authority, carry on insurance business in Brunei Darussalam as an insurance broker.\"; {b} by inserting the following new subsection immediately after\n\n(1) - \"(1A) Such person shall not be registered by the Authority unless {a} it is a company defined in the Companies Act (Chapter 39); (b} it has such minimum paid-up share capital as may be {c} it has such professional indemnity insurance as may be and {d} the Authority has been furnished with such documents and may be prescribed or as he may require in any particular case.\"; {c} in subsection (4), by inserting \"annual and registration\" immediately {d) by inserting the following new subsection immediately after\n\n(5) - \"(5A) The Authority shall cause notice of any registration or the any registration of an insurance broker to be published in the Gazette.\"; {e} by deleting subsection (8) and by substituting the following new therefor - \"(8) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) or (1A) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\". I st. 2015"}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A33","no":33,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 33."},"text":{"en":"Section 54 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (3), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $10,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both\" and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A34","no":34,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 34."},"text":{"en":"Section 55 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (1), by deleting \"Banking Act (Chapter 95), the Islamic Banking Act (Chapter 168)\" from the last 2 and by substituting \"Banking Order, 2006 (S 45/2006), the Islamic Banking Order, 2008 (S 98/2008)\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A35","no":35,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 35."},"text":{"en":"Section 56 of the principal Order is repealed and the following new section therefor - of adjusters."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36."},"text":{"en":"Section 57 of the principal Order is amended by deleting subsection (2) and by substituting the following new subsection therefor - \"(2} Any person who wilfully refuse to submit his books, accounts and or to allow the inspection thereof shall be guilty of an offence and be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both, and in the case of a continuing further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A37","no":37,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 37."},"text":{"en":"Section 59 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new immediately after subsection ( 12} - \"(13} Any or registered insurance broker who fails to with any provision of this section shall be guilty of an offence and be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day which the offence continues after conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A38","no":38,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 38."},"text":{"en":"Section 60 of the principal Order is amended -\n\n(a) in subsection (1), by deleting \"a qualified\" from the third line and by therefor;.\n\n(b) by adding the new immediately after {4} \"(5) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day during which the offence continues after"}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A39","no":39,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 39."},"text":{"en":"Section 62 of the principal Order is amended - fa) in subsection (1), in the proviso by deleting \"excepted\" from the second and by substituting \"exempted\" therefor;\n\nDARUSSALAM GOVERNMENT GAZETTE (b} in subsection (2), in the proviso by deleting \"excepted\" from the first last line and by substituting \"exempted\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A40","no":40,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 40."},"text":{"en":"Section 63 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new immediately after subsection (4) - \"(5) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A41","no":41,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 41."},"text":{"en":"Section 64 of the principal Order is amended - {a) in subsection (5), by deleting \"a fine not exceeding $10,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day which the offence continues after conviction\" and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $50,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction\" therefor;\n\n(b) by re-numbering the last 2 subsections as \"5\" and \"6\" respectively."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A42","no":42,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 42."},"text":{"en":"Section 65 of the principal Order is amended by deleting subsection (3) and by substituting the following new subsection therefor - \"(3) Any insurer which fails to comply with any direction made under\n\n(1) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day during which the offence continues conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A43","no":43,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 43."},"text":{"en":"Section 69 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new immediately after subsection (13) - \"(14) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not day during which the offence continues after conviction.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A44","no":44,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 44."},"text":{"en":"Section 71 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (2L by deleting \"a qualified\" from the first two lines and by substituting \"an\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A45","no":45,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 45."},"text":{"en":"Section 75 of the principal Order is amended by adding the following new immediately after subsection (3) \"(4) Any person who fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000.\". of new section 77B."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A46","no":46,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 46."},"text":{"en":"No person shall carry on insurance business in Brunei Darussalam as an insurance agent for any insurer not entitled under this Order to carry on in question in Brunei Darussalam and any person who contravenes this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $4,000 for every day during which the offence continues after Amendment of section 48."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A47","no":47,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 47."},"text":{"en":"Section 78 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (2), by deleting not exceeding $5,000, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day during which the offence continues after and by substituting \"a fine not exceeding $10,000, and in the case of a offence to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day during the offence continues after conviction\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A48","no":48,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 48."},"text":{"en":"Section 80 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (3L by inserting \"on\" immediately after \"or\" in the penultimate line."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A49","no":49,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 49."},"text":{"en":"Section 85 of the principal Order, is amended(a} in subsection (2) -\n\n(i) by deleting \", notwithstanding Part IX of the Stamp Act (Chapter 34),\" from the third line;\n\n(ii) without the policy moneys having been included in such a schedule or certificate as is mentioned in that subsection\" from the last 2 lines; (b} in subsection (3), by deleting \"of the payment\" fro;m.the second line."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A50","no":50,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 50."},"text":{"en":"Section 90 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (2), by inserting such later date as the Authority may in any particular case determine\" after \"months\" in the first line. of First Schedule."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A51","no":51,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 51."},"text":{"en":"The First Schedule to the principal Order is amended by deleting Parts I and III. of Third Schedule."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A52","no":52,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 52."},"text":{"en":"The Third Schedule to the principal Order is amended, in paragraph 8, by deleting \"Banking Act (Chapter 95), the Islamic Banking Act (Chapter 168)\" from the first 2 lines and by substituting \"Banking Order, 2006 (S 45/2006), the Islamic 2008 (S 96/2008)\" therefor. of Fourth Schedule."}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A53","no":53,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 53."},"text":{"en":"The Fourth Schedule to the principal Order is amended - (a} in Part I, in paragraph 1(2)fa/, by deleting \"60 and 61\" from the last line and by substituting \"5(2)fbJ and (c)\" therefor;\n\n(b) in Part III, in paragraph 6\n\n(i) by deleting \"6\" from the first line and by substituting \"3\" therefor;\n\n(ii) by deleting \"9\" from the third line and by substituting \"6\" therefor;\n\n(iii) by deleting \"6\" from the penultimate line and by substituting \"3\" Made lhis 6th. day of Ramadhan, 1436 Hijriah corresponding to the 23rd. day of June, 2015 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN\n\nBRUNEI DARUSSALAM"}},{"id":"BN-S-38-2015-E-INSURANCE-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2015-A56","no":56,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 56."},"text":{"en":"(1) No person shall, without being registered by the Authority, act or hold himself out as an adjuster. [2) Such person shall not be registered by the Authority unless {a} he is a member of an association of adjusters; {b} he has such minimum paid-up share capital as may be and (c} the Authority has been furnished with such documents and as may be prescribed or as he may require in any case.\n\n(3) In registering an adjuster, the Authority may impose such as he thinks fit any may at any time add to, vary or revoke such\n\n(4) The registration of an adjuster shall be for a period of one year and be renewable every year.\n\n(5) Adjusters shall pay such registration and annual fees as may be\n\n(6) The Authority shall cause notice of any registration or the any registration of an adjuster to be published in the Gazette.\n\n(7) The Authority may revoke the registration of any adjuster if he is that any of the conditions imposed in relation to the registration has been breached or that it is in the interests of the public for him to do so.\n\n(8) Nothing in this section shall apply to - {a) advocates and solicitors and members of other professions who act or assist in adjusting insurance claims as an incident to the their professions and who do not hold themselves out as {b) adjusters of maritime losses; {c) employees of an insurer who, in the course of their act or assist in adjusting insurance claims and who do not out as adjusters.\n\n(9) adjuster shall within one month after the end of each of the year submit to the Authority a report in the prescribed form of which were the subject of adjustments effected by him during that ( 10) Sections 40 to 45 shall apply to adjusters. {11) No person who carries on the business of an insurance loss adjuster, loss assessor, surveyor or other registered persons providing auxiliary services to the insurance industry or any member of their family, shall hold shares or other interests. in an insurance {12) For the purpose of subsection (11), \"member of their immediate includes any wife, husband, father, mother, son and daughter of a loss adjuster, loss assessor, surveyor or other registered persons providing auxiliary services to the insurance industry. {13) Any person who contravenes subsection {1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $800 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\n\n(14) Where a person fails to submit a report as required by subsection\n\n(9), he shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction.\""}}],"pack":"bn-p28","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"INSURANCE AMENDMENT ORDER 2015","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
